diamond
------------------------------------------
DIAMOND is a sequence aligner for protein and translated DNA searches and
functions as a drop-in replacement for the NCBI BLAST software tools. It is
suitable for protein-protein search as well as DNA-protein search on short
reads and longer sequences including contigs and assemblies, providing a
speedup of BLAST ranging up to x20,000.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libsqlite3_0-3.49.1-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libzstd1-1.5.7-1
  zlib0-1.3.2-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.4-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libsqlite3-devel-3.49.1-1
  libzstd-devel-1.5.7-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  zlib-devel-1.3.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/bbuchfink/diamond/

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/bbuchfink/diamond/archive/refs/tags/v2.2.8.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack diamond-2.2.8-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./diamond-2.2.8-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/diamond-2.2.8-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/diamond-2.2.8-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(diamond)
  /usr/bin/diamond.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/diamond.README
  /usr/share/doc/diamond/ChangeLog
  /usr/share/doc/diamond/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/diamond/README.md
  /usr/share/doc/diamond/TRADEMARKS

